  <revision rev="4" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>15cdc967cb5fec642a582aa619db45da</srcmd5>
    <version>1.19.30</version>
    <time>1786978755</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update mihomo to 1.19.30 (upstream release 2026-08-16).

Highlights:
- CVE-2026-56862 (boo#1275032): post-handshake TLS handshake messages such
  as KeyUpdate were always treated as state-advancing, so a malicious client
  could force unbounded key derivation on the server. mihomo statically links
  its own crypto/tls fork, so a fixed system Go would not have covered it;
  1.19.30 bumps that fork to metacubex/tls 0.1.8, which carries the fix.
- New ZeroTier outbound and a new &quot;mipstack&quot; userspace network stack
  (selectable via a new &quot;ip-stack&quot; option), AmneziaWG v3.0/v3.1 support,
  a substantially reworked sniffer, and DNS/OpenVPN/Tailscale fixes.

Packaging changes:
- License widened to &quot;GPL-3.0-only AND MPL-2.0&quot;. The Go binary statically
  links its vendored module set; the two new modules (metacubex/zerotier-go,
  metacubex/mipstack) are MPL-2.0, as are the already-linked
  metacubex/yamux and hashicorp/golang-lru. The linked set was derived with
  &quot;go list -deps&quot; for linux/amd64+arm64 with -tags with_gvisor and mapped
  onto vendor/modules.txt; the reasoning is recorded as a
  Legal-Review-Notice above the License tag. All other linked copyleft is
  GPL-3.0-or-later and is absorbed by GPL-3.0-only.
- %check now runs the upstream in-module unit test suite (55 packages &quot;ok&quot;)
  instead of only a version smoke test. The three listener/inbound
  *V2RayInterop tests are skipped because they shell out to
  &quot;go get github.com/v2fly/v2ray-core/v5&quot; to build a v2ray binary at test
  time, which cannot work in the offline build root; the separate test/
  directory is its own module driving docker and is never reached by ./... .
  The check asserts a minimum number of passing packages, because a suite
  that collects nothing also exits 0.
- golang(API) BuildRequires floor raised 1.20 -&gt; 1.21, which is what
  &quot;go test -skip&quot; needs.

Vendored Go modules regenerated via the go_modules source service:
138 -&gt; 135 modules (2 added, 5 removed, 17 updated).

No patches in this package, so none to rebase or drop.

Built and tested locally against openSUSE_Factory/aarch64.</comment>
    <requestid>1371504</requestid>
  </revision>
